#: about/troubleshooting.rst:2
#: development/compiling/compiling_for_windows.rst:241
#: development/editor/creating_icons.rst:89
#: tutorials/export/one-click_deploy.rst:61
#: tutorials/inputs/controllers_gamepads_joysticks.rst:174
#: tutorials/platforms/android/android_plugin.rst:146
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: about/troubleshooting.rst:4
msgid ""
"This page lists common issues encountered when using Rebel Engine and "
"possible solutions."
msgstr ""

#: about/troubleshooting.rst:7
msgid ""
"Everything I do in the editor or project manager appears delayed by one "
"frame."
msgstr ""

#: about/troubleshooting.rst:9
msgid ""
"This is a `known bug <https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/23069>`__ "
"on Intel graphics drivers on Windows. Updating to the latest graphics driver "
"version *provided by Intel* should fix the issue."
msgstr ""

#: about/troubleshooting.rst:13
msgid ""
"You should use the graphics driver provided by Intel rather than the one "
"provided by your desktop or laptop's manufacturer because their version is "
"often outdated."
msgstr ""

#: about/troubleshooting.rst:18
msgid ""
"The grid disappears and meshes turn black when I rotate the 3D camera in the "
"editor."
msgstr ""

#: about/troubleshooting.rst:20
msgid ""
"This is a `known bug <https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/30330>`__ "
"on Intel graphics drivers on Windows."
msgstr ""

#: about/troubleshooting.rst:23
msgid ""
"The only workaround, for now, is to switch to the GLES2 renderer. You can "
"switch the renderer in the top-right corner of the editor or the Project "
"Settings."
msgstr ""

#: about/troubleshooting.rst:26
msgid ""
"If you use a computer allowing you to switch your graphics card, like NVIDIA "
"Optimus, you can use the dedicated graphics card to run Rebel Engine."
msgstr ""

#: about/troubleshooting.rst:30
msgid "The editor or project takes a very long time to start."
msgstr ""

#: about/troubleshooting.rst:32
msgid ""
"This is a `known bug <https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/20566>`__ "
"on Windows when you have specific USB peripherals connected. In particular, "
"Corsair's iCUE software seems to cause the bug. Try updating your USB "
"peripherals' drivers to their latest version. If the bug persists, you need "
"to disconnect the faulty peripherals before opening the editor. You can then "
"connect the peripheral again."
msgstr ""

#: about/troubleshooting.rst:40
msgid ""
"Editor tooltips in the Inspector and Node docks blink when they're displayed."
msgstr ""

#: about/troubleshooting.rst:42
msgid ""
"This is a `known issue <https://github.com/godotengine/godot/"
"issues/32990>`__ caused by the third-party Stardock Fences application on "
"Windows. The only known workaround is to disable Stardock Fences while using "
"Rebel Engine."
msgstr ""

#: about/troubleshooting.rst:47
msgid ""
"The Rebel Engine editor appears frozen after clicking the system console."
msgstr ""

#: about/troubleshooting.rst:49
msgid ""
"When running Rebel Engine on Windows with the system console enabled, you "
"can accidentally enable *selection mode* by clicking inside the command "
"window. This Windows-specific behavior pauses the application to let you "
"select text inside the system console. Rebel Engine cannot override this "
"system-specific behavior."
msgstr ""

#: about/troubleshooting.rst:54
msgid ""
"To solve this, select the system console window and press Enter to leave "
"selection mode."
msgstr ""

#: about/troubleshooting.rst:58
msgid ""
"Some text such as \"NO DC\" appears in the top-left corner of the project "
"manager and editor window."
msgstr ""

#: about/troubleshooting.rst:60
msgid ""
"This is caused by the NVIDIA graphics driver injecting an overlay to display "
"information."
msgstr ""

#: about/troubleshooting.rst:62
msgid ""
"To disable this overlay on Windows, restore your graphics driver settings to "
"the default values in the NVIDIA Control Panel."
msgstr ""

#: about/troubleshooting.rst:65
msgid ""
"To disable this overlay on Linux, open ``nvidia-settings``, go to **X Screen "
"0 > OpenGL Settings** then uncheck **Enable Graphics API Visual Indicator**."
msgstr ""

#: about/troubleshooting.rst:69
msgid "The project window appears blurry, unlike the editor."
msgstr ""

#: about/troubleshooting.rst:71
msgid ""
"Unlike the editor, the project isn't marked as DPI-aware by default. This is "
"done to improve performance, especially on integrated graphics, where "
"rendering 3D scenes in hiDPI is slow."
msgstr ""

#: about/troubleshooting.rst:75
msgid ""
"To resolve this, open **Project > Project Settings** and enable **Display > "
"Window > Dpi > Allow Hidpi**. On top of that, make sure your project is "
"configured to support :doc:`multiple resolutions </tutorials/rendering/"
"multiple_resolutions>`."
msgstr ""

#: about/troubleshooting.rst:80
msgid "The project window doesn't appear centered when I run the project."
msgstr ""

#: about/troubleshooting.rst:82
msgid ""
"This is a `known bug <https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/13017>`__. "
"To resolve this, open **Project > Project Settings** and enable **Display > "
"Window > Dpi > Allow Hidpi**. On top of that, make sure your project is "
"configured to support :doc:`multiple resolutions </tutorials/rendering/"
"multiple_resolutions>`."
msgstr ""

#: about/troubleshooting.rst:88
msgid ""
"The project works when run from the editor, but fails to load some files "
"when running from an exported copy."
msgstr ""

#: about/troubleshooting.rst:90
msgid ""
"This is usually caused by forgetting to specify a filter for non-resource "
"files in the Export dialog. By default, Rebel Engine will only include "
"actual *resources* into the PCK file. Some files commonly used, such as JSON "
"files, are not considered resources. For example, if you load ``test.json`` "
"in the exported project, you need to specify ``*.json`` in the non-resource "
"export filter. See :ref:`tutorials/export/exporting_projects:resource "
"options` for more information."
msgstr ""

#: about/troubleshooting.rst:97
msgid ""
"On Windows, this can also be due to :ref:`case sensitivity <tutorials/"
"best_practices/project_organization:Case sensitivity>` issues. If you "
"reference a resource in your script with a different case than on the "
"filesystem, loading will fail once you export the project. This is because "
"the virtual PCK filesystem is case-sensitive, while Windows's filesystem is "
"case-insensitive by default."
msgstr ""

#: about/what_is_rebel.rst:2
