"create the release and debug `Android build variants <https://developer."
"android.com/build/build-variants>`__ of the Rebel Engine Android templates, "
"the target option should be set to ``release_debug`` and ``release`` "
"respectively. See :doc:`introduction_to_the_buildsystem` for more "
"information on Rebel Engine targets. For example, to compile Rebel Engine "
"for Android targeting the ``release`` (arm64-v8a) build variant run:"
msgstr ""

#: development/compiling/build_for_android.rst:74
msgid ""
"Rebel Engine can be compiled for the following `Android ABIs <https://"
"developer.android.com/ndk/guides/abis>`__:"
msgstr ""

#: development/compiling/build_for_android.rst:76
msgid "armeabi-v7a"
msgstr ""

#: development/compiling/build_for_android.rst:77
msgid "arm64-v8a"
msgstr ""

#: development/compiling/build_for_android.rst:78
msgid "x86"
msgstr ""

#: development/compiling/build_for_android.rst:79
msgid "x86_64"
msgstr ""

#: development/compiling/build_for_android.rst:81
msgid ""
"You specify the target Android ABI using the ``android_arch`` option with "
"``armv7``, ``arm64v8``, ``x86`` or ``x86_64``. For example, to compile Rebel "
"Engine for Android targeting the ``release`` variant and the ``armeabi-v7a`` "
"ABI run:"
msgstr ""

#: development/compiling/build_for_android.rst:90
msgid ""
"Almost all ARMv7 Android devices support `Neon <https://developer.android."
"com/ndk/guides/cpu-arm-neon>`__. Therefore, Neon is enabled by default, and "
"all pre-built Rebel Engine Android templates have Neon enabled. To support "
"an ARMv7 device that does not support Neon, you will need to build Rebel "
"Engine for Android ARMv7 with Neon disabled. Add the ``android_neon=false`` "
"option when targeting ``android_arch=armv7``."
msgstr ""

#: development/compiling/build_for_android.rst:97
msgid ""
"Rebel Engine for Android is built to support all devices running Android 5 "
"(Lollipop) and above. Android 5 was released in 2014, and Rebel Engine "
"supports 99.5% of all Android devices. Android 5 requires a minimum Android "
"SDK/API of 21. If you are compiling Rebel Engine for Android to add "
"functionality only available in a newer SDK/API, you can set the NDK minimum "
"Android SDK/API supported using the ``android_ndk_api`` option. For example, "
"to use a minimum Android SDK of 29 (Android 10 and newer devices only), use "
"``android_ndk_api=29``."
msgstr ""

#: development/compiling/build_for_android.rst:104
msgid ""
"The Rebel Engine Android templates contain both the ``release`` and "
"``release_debug`` build variants for each of the Android ABIs. To compile "
"the full suite of Android variants you will need to compile Rebel Engine for "
"Android 8 times:"
msgstr ""

#: development/compiling/build_for_android.rst:118
msgid ""
"The Rebel Engine build system will automatically copy the compiled Rebel "
"Engine library into the correct Android project folder. The Rebel Engine "
"build system will also automatically copy the desired ABI's ``libc++_shared."
"so`` library into the correct Android project folder."
msgstr ""

#: development/compiling/build_for_android.rst:122
msgid "Create the Rebel Engine Android templates"
msgstr ""

#: development/compiling/build_for_android.rst:124
msgid ""
"Rebel Engine Android templates are created using `Gradle tasks <https://docs."
"gradle.org/current/userguide/tutorial_using_tasks.html>`__."
msgstr ""

#: development/compiling/build_for_android.rst:127
msgid ""
"Rebel Engine source files include the `Gradle wrapper <https://docs.gradle."
"org/current/userguide/gradle_wrapper.html>`__, so you do not need to install "
"the `Gradle build software <https://gradle.org/>`__."
msgstr ""

#: development/compiling/build_for_android.rst:130
msgid ""
"To create the Rebel Engine Android templates, change to the ``platforms/"
"android/project`` directory and run the ``createAndroidTemplates`` Gradle "
"task:"
msgstr ""

#: development/compiling/build_for_android.rst:155
msgid ""
"The ``createAndroidTemplates`` task creates Android package (APK) templates "
"that will be updated by Rebel Editor when exporting for Android. The "
"``createAndroidTemplates`` task detects whether any release or debug build "
"variants have been compiled. Rebel Engine Android APK templates will only be "
"created for build variants that have been compiled. The release APK template "
"is called ``android_release.apk``. The debug APK template is called "
"``android_debug.apk``. The created Rebel Engine Android APK template files "
"are copied into the Rebel Engine ``bin`` directory."
msgstr ""

#: development/compiling/build_for_android.rst:162
msgid ""
"The ``createAndroidTemplates`` task detects the Android ABIs for each build "
"variant that has been previously compiled. Rebel Engine Android template "
"APKs will automatically include the Rebel Engine libraries and required "
"shared libraries for all the ABIs that have been previously compiled."
msgstr ""

#: development/compiling/build_for_android.rst:165
msgid ""
"The ``createAndroidTemplates`` task will also create an Android project "
"template that can be used to create Rebel Engine Android custom builds. The "
"Rebel Engine Android project template includes the Rebel Engine library as "
"an Android archive (``.aar``) file for each build variant detected. Rebel "
"Engine library Android archive files will only be created for build variants "
"that have been previously compiled. The Rebel Engine Android project "
"template is compressed into a zip file called ``android_template.zip`` and "
"saved in the Rebel Engine ``bin`` directory."
msgstr ""

#: development/compiling/build_for_android.rst:170
msgid ""
"Finally, the ``createAndroidTemplates`` task will copy the created Rebel "
"Engine library Android archive files ``engine-release.aar`` and ``engine-"
"debug.aar`` into the ``bin`` directory."
msgstr ""

#: development/compiling/build_for_android.rst:174
msgid ""
"The ``createAndroidTemplates`` task will detect and include any previously "
"compiled Android variants in the templates. To avoid including old versions "
"of the library for variants that are not desired, before compiling the "
"variants to be included, first run:"
msgstr ""

#: development/compiling/build_for_android.rst:200
msgid ""
"The ``createAndroidTemplates`` task will strip debug symbols from the Rebel "
"Engine libraries. To keep the debug symbols use "
"``createDevelopmentAndroidTemplates`` instead:"
msgstr ""

#: development/compiling/build_for_android.rst:224
msgid "Apply the templates"
msgstr ""

#: development/compiling/build_for_android.rst:226
msgid ""
"The Rebel Engine Android templates that you created can be applied in two "
"ways:"
msgstr ""

#: development/compiling/build_for_android.rst:228
msgid "`Apply Rebel Engine Android templates to all games`_"
msgstr ""

#: development/compiling/build_for_android.rst:229
msgid "`Apply Rebel Engine Android templates to a single game`_"
msgstr ""

#: development/compiling/build_for_android.rst:232
msgid "Apply Rebel Engine Android templates to all games"
msgstr ""

#: development/compiling/build_for_android.rst:234
msgid ""
"The Rebel Engine Android templates you created can be applied to all games "
"by copying them into Rebel Editor's shared templates folder. To find the "
"Rebel Editor's shared templates folder, open Rebel Editor. From the Editor "
"menu, select ``Open Editor Data Folder``."
msgstr ""

#: development/compiling/build_for_android.rst:241
msgid "Rebel Editor's Editor menu's Open Editor Data Folder"
msgstr ""

