#: development/editor/creating_icons.rst:2
msgid "Editor icons"
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/creating_icons.rst:4
msgid ""
"When a new class is created and exposed to scripting, the editor's interface "
"will display it with a default icon representing the base class it inherits "
"from. In most cases, it's still recommended to create icons for new classes "
"to improve the user experience."
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/creating_icons.rst:10
msgid "Creating icons"
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/creating_icons.rst:12
msgid ""
"To create new icons, you first need a vector graphics editor installed. For "
"instance, you can use the open source `Inkscape <https://inkscape.org/>`__ "
"editor."
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/creating_icons.rst:15
msgid "Clone the ``RebelEngine`` repository containing all the editor icons:"
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/creating_icons.rst:21
msgid ""
"The icons must be created in a vector graphics editor in SVG format. There "
"are two main requirements to follow:"
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/creating_icons.rst:24
msgid ""
"Icons must be 16×16. In Inkscape, you can configure the document size in "
"**File > Document Properties**."
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/creating_icons.rst:26
msgid ""
"Lines should be snapped to pixels whenever possible to remain crisp at lower "
"DPI. You can create a 16×16 grid in Inkscape to make this easier."
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/creating_icons.rst:29
msgid ""
"Once you're satisfied with the icon's design, save the icon in the cloned "
"repository's ``editor/icons`` folder. The icon name should match the "
"intended name in a case-sensitive manner. For example, to create an icon for "
"CPUParticles2D, name the file ``CPUParticles2D.svg``."
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/creating_icons.rst:35
msgid "Color conversion for light editor themes"
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/creating_icons.rst:37
msgid ""
"If the user has configured their editor to use a light theme, Rebel Editor "
"will convert the icon's colors based on a set of predefined color mappings. "
"This is to ensure the icon always displays with a sufficient contrast rate. "
"Try to restrict your icon's color palette to colors found in the list above. "
"Otherwise, your icon may become difficult to read on a light background."
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/creating_icons.rst:44
msgid "Icon optimization"
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/creating_icons.rst:46
msgid ""
"Because the editor renders SVGs once at load time, they need to be small in "
"size so they can be efficiently parsed. Editor icons must be first optimized "
"before being added to the engine, to do so:"
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/creating_icons.rst:50
msgid ""
"Install `svgcleaner <https://github.com/RazrFalcon/svgcleaner>`__ by "
"downloading a binary from its `Releases tab <https://github.com/RazrFalcon/"
"svgcleaner/releases/latest>`__ and placing it into a location in your "
"``PATH`` environment variable."
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/creating_icons.rst:55
msgid ""
"Run the command below, replacing ``svg_source.svg`` with the path to your "
"SVG file (which can be a relative or absolute path):"
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/creating_icons.rst:62
msgid ""
"The ``--multipass`` switch improves compression, so make sure to include it. "
"The optimized icon will be saved to ``svg_optimized.svg``. You can also "
"change the destination parameter to any relative or absolute path you'd like."
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/creating_icons.rst:68
msgid ""
"While this optimization step won't impact the icon's quality noticeably, it "
"will still remove editor-only information such as guides. Therefore, it's "
"recommended to keep the source SVG around if you need to make further "
"changes."
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/creating_icons.rst:74
msgid "Integrating and sharing the icons"
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/creating_icons.rst:76
msgid ""
"If you're contributing to the engine itself, you should make a pull request "
"to add optimized icons to ``editor/icons`` in the main repository. Recompile "
"the engine to make it pick up new icons for classes."
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/creating_icons.rst:80
msgid ""
"It's also possible to create custom icons within a module. If you're "
"creating your own module and don't plan to integrate it with Rebel Engine, "
"you don't need to make a separate pull request for your icons to be "
"available within the editor as they can be self-contained."
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/creating_icons.rst:85
msgid ""
"For specific instructions on how to create module icons, refer to :ref:"
"`Creating custom module icons<development/engine/custom_modules_in_cpp:"
"adding custom editor icons>`."
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/creating_icons.rst:91
msgid "If icons don't appear in the editor, make sure that:"
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/creating_icons.rst:93
msgid ""
"Each icon's filename matches the naming requirement as described previously."
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/creating_icons.rst:95
msgid ""
"``modules/svg`` is enabled (it should be enabled by default). Without it, "
"icons won't appear in the editor at all."
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/creating_icons.rst:100
msgid ""
"`editor/icons <https://github.com/RebelToolbox/RebelEngine/tree/main/editor/"
"icons>`__"
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:2
msgid "Editor style guide"
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:7
msgid "Thanks for your interest in contributing to the Rebel Editor!"
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:9
msgid ""
"This page describes the grammar and writing style used throughout the Rebel "
"Editor. Following this style guide will help your contribution get merged "
"faster since there will be fewer review steps required."
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:14
msgid "Writing style"
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:16
msgid ""
"**Write messages (errors, warnings, …) as full sentences.** They should "
"start with an uppercase letter and end with a period."
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:18
msgid ""
"**Try to keep sentences short.** This makes it more likely that their "
"translations will be short as well, which is a good thing to avoid UI bugs."
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:20
msgid ""
"**Use contractions.** For example, use \"isn't\" instead of \"is not\". An "
"exception to this rule can be made when you specifically want to emphasize "
"one of the contraction's words."
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:23
msgid ""
"**Use double quotes in messages** (``\"\"``) instead of single quotes "
"(``''``). Double quotes should be used to quote user input, file paths and "
"possibly other things depending on the context."
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:29
msgid ""
"Try to follow the :doc:`/contributing/docs_writing_guidelines` in addition "
"to the guidelines outlined above."
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:33
msgid "Button and menu texts"
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:35
msgid "Capitalize text in buttons and menu actions:"
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:37
msgid "**Good:** *Open Editor Data Folder*"
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:38
msgid "**Bad:** *Open editor data folder*"
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:40
msgid ""
"If a menu action opens a modal dialog, suffix it with an ellipsis (``…``)."
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:42
msgid "**Good:** *Editor Settings…*"
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:43
msgid "**Bad:** *Editor Settings*"
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:46
msgid "Inspector sections"
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:48
msgid ""
"In general, don't create sections that contain less than 3 items. Sections "
"that contain few items make it difficult to navigate the inspector, while "
"missing the benefits of using sections such as folding."
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:52
msgid ""
"There are some valid exceptions for this, such as material features in :ref:"
"`class_SpatialMaterial`."
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:55
msgid "This advice also applies to the Project Settings and Editor Settings."
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:58
msgid "Inspector performance hints"
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:60
msgid ""
"Enum properties that noticeably impact performance should have a performance "
"hint associated. The hint should refer to the *absolute* performance impact, "
"rather than being relative to the other options provided in the enum. Here "
"are some examples taken from the Rebel Editor:"
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:65
msgid "**Screen-space antialiasing:** *Disabled (Fastest), FXAA (Fast)*"
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:66
msgid ""
"**MSAA quality:** *Disabled (Fastest), 2x (Fast), 4x (Average), 8x (Slow), "
"16x (Slower)*"
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:68
msgid ""
"**DirectionalLight mode:** *Orthogonal (Fast), PSSM 2 Splits (Average), PSSM "
"4 Splits (Slow)*"
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:71
msgid ""
"For consistency, try to stick to the terms below (from fastest to slowest):"
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:73
msgid "*Fastest, Faster, Fast, Average, Slow, Slower, Slowest*"
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:75
msgid ""
"Their usage doesn't have to be contiguous. For example, you can use only "
"\"Fast\" and \"Slow\" from the list above."
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:78
msgid ""
"If you're adding a new enum, its values should be ordered from the fastest "
"option to the slowest option."
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:82
msgid "Tooltips"
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:84
msgid ""
"Consider adding tooltips whenever the action performed by a button or menu "
"action isn't obvious. You can also provide additional context or highlight "
"caveats in the tooltip."
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:88
msgid ""
"You can do this by calling ``set_tooltip(TTR(\"Text here.\"))`` on the "
"Control-based node in question. If the tooltip is particularly long (more "
"than ~80 characters), wrap it over several lines by adding line breaks using "
"``\\n``."
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:92
msgid ""
"Tooltips should follow the writing style described above. In addition to "
"this, use indicative mood instead of imperative mood:"
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:95
msgid "**Good:** *Computes global illumination for the selected GIProbe.*"
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/editor_style_guide.rst:96
msgid "**Bad:** *Compute global illumination for the selected GIProbe.*"
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/index.rst:2
msgid "Editor development"
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/introduction_to_editor_development.rst:2
msgid "Introduction to editor development"
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/introduction_to_editor_development.rst:4
msgid "On this page, you will learn:"
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/introduction_to_editor_development.rst:6
msgid "The **design decisions** behind the Rebel Editor."
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/introduction_to_editor_development.rst:7
msgid "How to work efficiently on the Rebel Editor's C++ code."
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/introduction_to_editor_development.rst:9
msgid ""
"This guide is aimed at current or future engine contributors. To create "
"editor plugins in GDScript, see :doc:`/tutorials/plugins/editor/"
"making_plugins` instead."
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/introduction_to_editor_development.rst:14
msgid ""
"If you are new to Rebel, we recommended you to read :doc:`/getting_started/"
"introduction/design_philosophy` before continuing. Since the Rebel Editor is "
"a Rebel project written in C++, much of the engine's philosophy applies to "
"the editor."
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/introduction_to_editor_development.rst:20
msgid "Technical choices"
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/introduction_to_editor_development.rst:22
msgid ""
"The Rebel Editor is drawn using Rebel's renderer and :ref:`UI system <toc-"
"gui-basics>`. It does *not* rely on a toolkit such as GTK or Qt. This is "
"similar in spirit to software like Blender. While using toolkits makes it "
"easier to achieve a \"native\" appearance, they are also quite heavy and "
"their licensing is not compatible with Rebel Engine's."
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/introduction_to_editor_development.rst:28
msgid ""
"The editor is fully written in C++. It can't contain any GDScript or C# code."
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/introduction_to_editor_development.rst:31
msgid "Directory structure"
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/introduction_to_editor_development.rst:33
msgid ""
"The editor's code is fully self-contained in the `editor/ <https://github."
"com/RebelToolbox/RebelEngine/tree/main/editor>`__ folder of the Rebel Engine "
"source repository."
msgstr ""

#: development/editor/introduction_to_editor_development.rst:37
msgid ""
"Some editor functionality is also implemented via :doc:`modules </"
