#: development/engine/variant_class.rst:7
msgid ""
"Variant is the most important datatype of Rebel Engine, it's the most "
"important class in the engine. A Variant takes up only 20 bytes and can "
"store almost any engine datatype inside of it. Variants are rarely used to "
"hold information for long periods of time, instead they are used mainly for "
"communication, editing, serialization and generally moving data around."
msgstr ""

#: development/engine/variant_class.rst:14
msgid "A Variant can:"
msgstr ""

#: development/engine/variant_class.rst:16
msgid "Store almost any datatype"
msgstr ""

#: development/engine/variant_class.rst:17
msgid ""
"Perform operations between many variants (GDScript uses Variant as its "
"atomic/native datatype)."
msgstr ""

#: development/engine/variant_class.rst:19
msgid "Be hashed, so it can be compared quickly to other variants"
msgstr ""

#: development/engine/variant_class.rst:20
msgid "Be used to convert safely between datatypes"
msgstr ""

#: development/engine/variant_class.rst:21
msgid ""
"Be used to abstract calling methods and their arguments (Rebel Engine "
"exports all its functions through variants)"
msgstr ""

#: development/engine/variant_class.rst:23
msgid "Be used to defer calls or move data between threads."
msgstr ""

#: development/engine/variant_class.rst:24
msgid "Be serialized as binary and stored to disk, or transferred via network."
msgstr ""

#: development/engine/variant_class.rst:26
msgid ""
"Be serialized to text and use it for printing values and editable settings."
msgstr ""

#: development/engine/variant_class.rst:28
msgid "Work as an exported property, so the editor can edit it universally."
msgstr ""

#: development/engine/variant_class.rst:29
msgid "Be used for dictionaries, arrays, parsers, etc."
msgstr ""

#: development/engine/variant_class.rst:31
msgid ""
"Basically, thanks to the Variant class, writing Rebel Engine itself was a "
"much, much easier task, as it allows for highly dynamic constructs not "
"common of C++ with little effort. Become a friend of Variant today."
msgstr ""

#: development/engine/variant_class.rst:37
