#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:2
msgid "Exporting for the Web"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:6
msgid ""
"This page describes how to export a Rebel project to HTML5. If you're "
"looking to compile editor or export template binaries from source instead, "
"read :doc:`/development/compiling/compiling_for_web`."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:10
msgid ""
"HTML5 export allows publishing games made in Rebel Editor to the browser. "
"This requires support for `WebAssembly <https://webassembly.org/>`__ and "
"`WebGL <https://www.khronos.org/webgl/>`__ in the user's browser."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:15
msgid ""
"Use the browser-integrated developer console, usually opened with :kbd:"
"`F12`, to view **debug information** like JavaScript, engine, and WebGL "
"errors."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:19
msgid ""
"`There are significant bugs when running HTML5 projects on iOS <https://"
"github.com/godotengine/godot/issues?q=is:issue+is:open+label:platform:"
"html5+ios>`__ (regardless of the browser). We recommend using :doc:`iOS' "
"native export functionality </tutorials/export/exporting_for_ios>` instead, "
"as it will also result in better performance."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:26
msgid "WebGL version"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:28
msgid ""
"Depending on your choice of renderer, Rebel Engine can target WebGL 1.0 "
"(*GLES2*) or WebGL 2.0 (*GLES3*)."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:31
msgid ""
"WebGL 1.0 is the recommended option if you want your project to be supported "
"on all browsers with the best performance."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:34
msgid ""
"Rebel Engine's GLES3 renderer targets high end devices, and the performance "
"using WebGL 2.0 can be subpar. Some features are also not supported in WebGL "
"2.0 specifically."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:38
msgid ""
"Additionally, while most browsers support WebGL 2.0, this is not yet the "
"case for **Safari**. WebGL 2.0 support is coming in Safari 15 for macOS, and "
"is not available yet for any **iOS** browser (all WebKit-based like Safari). "
"See `Can I use WebGL 2.0 <https://caniuse.com/webgl2>`__ for details."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:44
msgid "Export options"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:46
msgid ""
"If a runnable web export template is available, a button appears between the "
"*Stop scene* and *Play edited Scene* buttons in the editor to quickly open "
"the game in the default browser for testing."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:50
msgid ""
"You can choose the **Export Type** to select which features will be "
"available:"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:52
msgid ""
"*Regular*: is the most compatible across browsers, will not support threads, "
"nor GDNative."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:54
msgid ""
"*Threads*: will require the browser to support `SharedArrayBuffer <https://"
"developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/"
"SharedArrayBuffer>`__. See `Can I use SharedArrayBuffer <https://caniuse.com/"
"sharedarraybuffer>`__ for details."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:58
msgid ""
"*GDNative*: enables GDNative support but makes the binary bigger and slower "
"to load."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:61
msgid ""
"If you plan to use :doc:`VRAM compression </tutorials/assets_pipeline/"
"importing_images>` make sure that **Vram Texture Compression** is enabled "
"for the targeted platforms (enabling both **For Desktop** and **For Mobile** "
"will result in a bigger, but more compatible export)."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:66
msgid ""
"If a path to a **Custom HTML shell** file is given, it will be used instead "
"of the default HTML page. See :doc:`/tutorials/platforms/"
"customizing_html5_shell`."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:69
msgid ""
"**Head Include** is appended into the ``<head>`` element of the generated "
"HTML page. This allows to, for example, load webfonts and third-party "
"JavaScript APIs, include CSS, or run JavaScript code."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:73
msgid ""
"Each project must generate their own HTML file. On export, several text "
"placeholders are replaced in the generated HTML file specifically for the "
"given export options. Any direct modifications to that HTML file will be "
"lost in future exports. To customize the generated file, use the **Custom "
"HTML shell** option."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:80
msgid ""
"**Export types** other then *Regular* are not yet supported by the C# "
"version."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:86
msgid ""
"For security and privacy reasons, many features that work effortlessly on "
"native platforms are more complicated on the web platform. Following is a "
"list of limitations you should be aware of when porting a Rebel game to the "
"web."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:91
msgid "Secure contexts"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:93
msgid ""
"Browser vendors are making more and more functionalities only available in "
"`secure contexts <https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Security/"
"Secure_Contexts>`__, this means that such features are only be available if "
"the web page is served via a secure HTTPS connection (localhost is usually "
"exempt from such requirement)."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:99
msgid ""
"Check the `list of open HTML5 issues on GitHub <https://github.com/"
"godotengine/godot/issues?q=is:open+is:issue+label:platform:html5>`__ to see "
"if the functionality you're interested in has an issue yet. If not, open one "
"to communicate your interest."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:105
msgid "Using cookies for data persistence"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:107
msgid ""
"Users must **allow cookies** (specifically IndexedDB) if persistence of the "
"``user://`` file system is desired. When playing a game presented in an "
"``iframe``, **third-party** cookies must also be enabled. Incognito/private "
"browsing mode also prevents persistence."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:112
msgid ""
"The method ``OS.is_userfs_persistent()`` can be used to check if the "
"``user://`` file system is persistent, but can give false positives in some "
"cases."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:117
msgid "Background processing"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:119
msgid ""
"The project will be paused by the browser when the tab is no longer the "
"active tab in the user's browser. This means functions such as "
"``_process()`` and ``_physics_process()`` will no longer run until the tab "
"is made active again by the user (by switching back to the tab). This can "
"cause networked games to disconnect if the user switches tabs for a long "
"duration."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:125
msgid ""
"This limitation does not apply to unfocused browser *windows*. Therefore, on "
"the user's side, this can be worked around by running the project in a "
"separate *window* instead of a separate tab."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:130
#: tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:196
#: tutorials/performance/threads/thread_safe_apis.rst:5
#: tutorials/performance/threads/using_multiple_threads.rst:5
msgid "Threads"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:132
msgid ""
"As mentioned :ref:`above <tutorials/export/exporting_for_web:Export "
"options>` multi-threading is only available if the appropriate **Export "
"Type** is set and support for it across browsers is still limited."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:136
msgid ""
"Requires a :ref:`secure context <tutorials/export/exporting_for_web:Secure "
"contexts>`. Browsers also require that the web page is served with specific "
"`cross-origin isolation headers <https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/"
"Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy>`__."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:141
#: tutorials/scripting/gdnative/index.rst:2
msgid "GDNative"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:143
msgid ""
"As mentioned :ref:`above <tutorials/export/exporting_for_web:Export "
"options>` GDNative is only available if the appropriate **Export Type** is "
"set."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:146
msgid ""
"The export will also copy the required GDNative ``.wasm`` files to the "
"output folder (and must be uploaded to your server along with your game)."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:150
msgid "Full screen and mouse capture"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:152
msgid ""
"Browsers do not allow arbitrarily **entering full screen**. The same goes "
"for **capturing the cursor**. Instead, these actions have to occur as a "
"response to a JavaScript input event. In Rebel Engine, this means entering "
"full screen from within a pressed input event callback such as ``_input`` or "
"``_unhandled_input``. Querying the :ref:`class_Input` singleton is not "
"sufficient, the relevant input event must currently be active."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:159
msgid ""
"For the same reason, the full screen project setting doesn't work unless the "
"engine is started from within a valid input event handler. This requires :"
"doc:`customization of the HTML page </tutorials/platforms/"
"customizing_html5_shell>`."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:166
msgid ""
"Chrome restricts how websites may play audio. It may be necessary for the "
"player to click or tap or press a key to enable audio."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:169
msgid ""
"Google offers additional information about their `Web Audio autoplay "
"policies <https://developer.chrome.com/blog/web-audio-autoplay/>`__."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:172
msgid ""
"Access to microphone requires a :ref:`secure context <tutorials/export/"
"exporting_for_web:Secure contexts>`."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:178
msgid ""
"Low level networking is not implemented due to lacking support in browsers."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:180
msgid ""
"Currently, only :doc:`HTTP client </tutorials/networking/"
"http_client_class>`, :doc:`HTTP requests </tutorials/networking/"
"http_request_class>`, :doc:`WebSocket (client) </tutorials/networking/"
"websocket>` and :doc:`WebRTC </tutorials/networking/webrtc>` are supported."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:185
msgid "The HTTP classes also have several restrictions on the HTML5 platform:"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:187
msgid "Accessing or changing the ``StreamPeer`` is not possible"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:188
msgid "Threaded/Blocking mode is not available"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:189
msgid ""
"Cannot progress more than once per frame, so polling in a loop will freeze"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:190
msgid "No chunked responses"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:191
msgid "Host verification cannot be disabled"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:192
msgid ""
"Subject to `same-origin policy <https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/"
"Security/Same-origin_policy>`__"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:195
msgid "Clipboard"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:197
msgid ""
"Clipboard synchronization between engine and the operating system requires a "
"browser supporting the `Clipboard API <https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/"
"docs/Web/API/Clipboard_API>`__, additionally, due to the API asynchronous "
"nature might not be reliable when accessed from GDScript."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:202
#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:213
msgid ""
"Requires a :ref:`secure context <tutorials/export/exporting_for_web:Secure "
"contexts>`."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:205
msgid "Gamepads"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:207
msgid ""
"Gamepads will not be detected until one of their button is pressed. Gamepads "
"might have the wrong mapping depending on the browser/OS/gamepad "
"combination, sadly the `Gamepad API <https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/"
"docs/Web/API/Gamepad_API/Using_the_Gamepad_API>`__ does not provide a "
"reliable way to detect the gamepad information necessary to remap them based "
"on model/vendor/OS due to privacy considerations."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:216
msgid "Boot splash is not displayed"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:218
msgid ""
"The default HTML page does not display the boot splash while loading. "
"However, the image is exported as a PNG file, so :doc:`custom HTML pages </"
"tutorials/platforms/customizing_html5_shell>` can display it."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:223
msgid "Shader language limitations"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:225
#: tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:374
msgid ""
"When exporting a GLES2 project to HTML5, WebGL 1.0 will be used. WebGL 1.0 "
"doesn't support dynamic loops, so shaders using those won't work there."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:229
msgid "Serving the files"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:231
msgid ""
"Exporting for the web generates several files to be served from a web "
"server, including a default HTML page for presentation. A custom HTML file "
"can be used, see :doc:`/tutorials/platforms/customizing_html5_shell`."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:235
msgid ""
"The generated ``.html`` file can be used as ``DirectoryIndex`` in Apache "
"servers and can be renamed to e.g. ``index.html`` at any time, its name is "
"never depended on by default."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:239
msgid ""
"The HTML page draws the game at maximum size within the browser window. This "
"way it can be inserted into an ``<iframe>`` with the game's size, as is "
"common on most web game hosting sites."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:243
msgid ""
"The other exported files are served as they are, next to the ``.html`` file, "
"names unchanged. The ``.wasm`` file is a binary WebAssembly module "
"implementing the engine. The ``.pck`` file is the Rebel main pack containing "
"your game. The ``.js`` file contains start-up code and is used by the ``."
"html`` file to access the engine. The ``.png`` file contains the boot splash "
"image. It is not used in the default HTML page, but is included for :doc:"
"`custom HTML pages </tutorials/platforms/customizing_html5_shell>`."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:251
msgid ""
"The ``.pck`` file is binary, usually delivered with the MIME-type :mimetype:"
"`application/octet-stream`. The ``.wasm`` file is delivered as :mimetype:"
"`application/wasm`."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:255
msgid ""
"Delivering the WebAssembly module (``.wasm``) with a MIME-type other than :"
"mimetype:`application/wasm` can prevent some start-up optimizations."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:259
msgid ""
"Delivering the files with server-side compression is recommended especially "
"for the ``.pck`` and ``.wasm`` files, which are usually large in size. The "
"WebAssembly module compresses particularly well, down to around a quarter of "
"its original size with gzip compression."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:264
msgid "**Hosts that provide on-the-fly compression:** GitHub Pages (gzip)"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:266
msgid ""
"**Hosts that don't provide on-the-fly compression:** itch.io, GitLab Pages "
"(`supports manual gzip precompression <https://webd97.de/posts/gitlab-pages-"
"compression/>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:270
msgid "Calling JavaScript from script"
msgstr ""

