#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:300
msgid ""
"HTML5 export templates may be :doc:`built </development/compiling/"
"compiling_for_web>` without support for the singleton to improve security. "
"With such templates, and on platforms other than HTML5, calling ``JavaScript."
"eval`` will also return ``null``. The availability of the singleton can be "
"checked with the ``JavaScript`` :doc:`feature tag </tutorials/export/"
"feature_tags>`::"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:314
msgid ""
"GDScript's multi-line strings, surrounded by 3 quotes ``\"\"\"`` as in "
"``my_func3()`` above, are useful to keep JavaScript code readable."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.rst:317
msgid ""
"The ``eval`` method also accepts a second, optional Boolean argument, which "
"specifies whether to execute the code in the global execution context, "
"defaulting to ``false`` to prevent polluting the global namespace::"
