#: tutorials/i18n/localization_using_gettext.rst:2
msgid "Localization using gettext"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/i18n/localization_using_gettext.rst:4
msgid ""
"In addition to :doc:`/tutorials/assets_pipeline/importing_translations` in "
"CSV format, Rebel Engine also supports loading translation files written in "
"the GNU gettext (``.po``) format."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/i18n/localization_using_gettext.rst:8
msgid ""
"For an introduction to gettext, check out `A Quick Gettext Tutorial <https://"
"www.labri.fr/perso/fleury/posts/programming/a-quick-gettext-tutorial."
"html>`__. It's written with C projects in mind, but much of the advice also "
"applies to Rebel Engine (with the exception of ``xgettext``)."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/i18n/localization_using_gettext.rst:14
msgid "Advantages"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/i18n/localization_using_gettext.rst:16
msgid ""
"gettext is a standard format, which can be edited using any text editor or "
"GUI editors such as `Poedit <https://poedit.net/>`__."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/i18n/localization_using_gettext.rst:18
msgid ""
"gettext is supported by translation platforms such as `Transifex <https://"
"www.transifex.com/>`__ and `Weblate <https://weblate.org/>`__, which makes "
"it easier for people to collaborate to localization."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/i18n/localization_using_gettext.rst:21
msgid ""
"Compared to CSV, gettext works better with version control systems like Git, "
"as each locale has its own messages file."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/i18n/localization_using_gettext.rst:23
msgid ""
"Multiline strings are more convenient to edit in gettext files compared to "
"CSV files."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/i18n/localization_using_gettext.rst:27
msgid "Disadvantages"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/i18n/localization_using_gettext.rst:29
msgid ""
"gettext is a more complex format than CSV and can be harder to grasp for "
"people new to software localization."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/i18n/localization_using_gettext.rst:31
msgid ""
"People who maintain localization files will have to install gettext tools on "
"their system. However, as Rebel Engine doesn't use compiled message object "
"files (``.mo``), translators can test their work without having to install "
"gettext tools."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/i18n/localization_using_gettext.rst:37
msgid "Caveats"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/i18n/localization_using_gettext.rst:39
msgid ""
"As Rebel Engine uses its own PO file parser behind the scenes (which is more "
"limited than the reference GNU gettext implementation), some features such "
"as pluralization aren't supported."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/i18n/localization_using_gettext.rst:44
msgid "Installing gettext tools"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/i18n/localization_using_gettext.rst:46
msgid ""
"The command line gettext tools are required to perform maintenance "
"operations, such as updating message files. Therefore, it's strongly "
"recommended to install them."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/i18n/localization_using_gettext.rst:50
msgid ""
"**Windows:** Download an installer from `this page <https://mlocati.github."
"io/articles/gettext-iconv-windows.html>`__. Any architecture and binary type "
"(shared or static) works; if in doubt, choose the 64-bit static installer."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/i18n/localization_using_gettext.rst:54
msgid ""
"**macOS:** Install gettext either using `Homebrew <https://brew.sh/>`__ with "
"the ``brew install gettext`` command, or using `MacPorts <https://www."
"macports.org/>`__ with the ``sudo port install gettext`` command."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/i18n/localization_using_gettext.rst:58
msgid ""
"**Linux:** On most distributions, install the ``gettext`` package from your "
"distribution's package manager."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/i18n/localization_using_gettext.rst:62
msgid "Creating the PO template (POT) manually"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/i18n/localization_using_gettext.rst:64
msgid ""
"Rebel Engine currently doesn't support extracting source strings using "
"``xgettext``, so the ``.pot`` file must be created manually. This file can "
"be placed anywhere in the project directory, but it's recommended to keep it "
"in a subdirectory, as each locale will be defined in its own file."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/i18n/localization_using_gettext.rst:69
msgid ""
"Create a directory named `locale` in the project directory. In this "
"directory, save a file named ``messages.pot`` with the following contents:"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/i18n/localization_using_gettext.rst:81
msgid ""
"Messages in gettext are made of ``msgid`` and ``msgstr`` pairs. ``msgid`` is "
"the source string (usually in English), ``msgstr`` will be the translated "
"string."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/i18n/localization_using_gettext.rst:85
msgid ""
"The ``msgstr`` value in PO template files (``.pot``) should **always** be "
"empty. Localization will be done in the generated ``.po`` files instead."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/i18n/localization_using_gettext.rst:89
