#: tutorials/io/data_paths.rst:2
msgid "File paths in Rebel projects"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/io/data_paths.rst:4
msgid ""
"This page explains how file paths work inside Rebel projects. You will learn "
"how to access paths in your projects using the ``res://`` and ``user://`` "
"notations and where Rebel stores user files on your hard-drive."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/io/data_paths.rst:9
msgid "Path separators"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/io/data_paths.rst:11
msgid ""
"To make supporting multiple platforms easier, Rebel Engine only accepts UNIX-"
"style path separators (``/``). These work on all platforms, **including "
"Windows**."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/io/data_paths.rst:14
msgid ""
"Instead of writing paths like ``C:\\Projects``, in Rebel Editor, you should "
"write ``C:/Projects``."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/io/data_paths.rst:18
msgid "Accessing files in the project folder"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/io/data_paths.rst:20
msgid ""
"Rebel Editor considers that a project exists in any folder that contains a "
"``project.rebel`` text file, even if the file is empty. The folder that "
"contains this file is your project's root folder."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/io/data_paths.rst:24
msgid ""
"You can access any file relative to it by writing paths starting with "
"``res://``, which stands for resources. For example, you can access an image "
"file ``character.png`` located in the project's root folder in code with the "
"following path: ``res://character.png``."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/io/data_paths.rst:30
msgid "Accessing persistent user data"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/io/data_paths.rst:32
msgid ""
"To store persistent data files, like the player's save or settings, you want "
"to use ``user://`` instead of ``res://`` as your path's prefix. This is "
"because when the game is running, the project's file system will likely be "
"read-only."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/io/data_paths.rst:36
msgid ""
"The ``user://`` prefix points to a different directory on the user's device. "
"Unlike ``res://``, the directory pointed at by ``user://`` is *guaranteed* "
"to be writable to, even in an exported project."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/io/data_paths.rst:40
msgid "On desktop platforms, the actual directory paths for ``user://`` are:"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/io/data_paths.rst:45 tutorials/io/data_paths.rst:73
msgid "User data"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/io/data_paths.rst:45 tutorials/io/data_paths.rst:73
msgid "Windows: ``%APPDATA%\\Rebel\\app_userdata\\[project_name]``"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/io/data_paths.rst:46
msgid ""
"macOS: ``~/Library/Application Support/Rebel/app_userdata/[project_name]``"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/io/data_paths.rst:47
msgid "Linux: ``~/.local/share/rebel/app_userdata/[project_name]``"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/io/data_paths.rst:49 tutorials/io/data_paths.rst:77
msgid "User data (when ``use_custom_user_dir`` project setting is ``true``)"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/io/data_paths.rst:49 tutorials/io/data_paths.rst:77
msgid "Windows: ``%APPDATA%\\[project_name]``"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/io/data_paths.rst:50 tutorials/io/data_paths.rst:78
msgid "macOS: ``~/Library/Application Support/[project_name]``"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/io/data_paths.rst:51 tutorials/io/data_paths.rst:79
msgid "Linux: ``~/.local/share/[project_name]``"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/io/data_paths.rst:54
msgid ""
"``[project_name]`` is based on the application name defined in the Project "
"Settings, but you can override it on a per-platform basis using :doc:"
"`feature tags </tutorials/export/feature_tags>`."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/io/data_paths.rst:57
msgid ""
"On mobile platforms, this path is unique to the project and is not "
"accessible by other applications for security reasons."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/io/data_paths.rst:60
msgid ""
"On HTML5 exports, ``user://`` will refer to a virtual filesystem stored on "
"the device via IndexedDB. (Interaction with the main filesystem can still be "
"performed through the :ref:`JavaScript <class_JavaScript>` singleton.)"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/io/data_paths.rst:65
msgid "Editor data paths"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/io/data_paths.rst:67
msgid ""
"The editor uses different paths for user data, user settings, and cache, "
"depending on the platform. By default, these paths are:"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/io/data_paths.rst:74
msgid "macOS: ``~/Library/Application Support/Rebel/[project_name]``"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/io/data_paths.rst:75
msgid "Linux: ``~/.local/share/rebel/[project_name]``"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/io/data_paths.rst:81
