#: tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_basics.rst:161
msgid ""
"If you see an error like \"Unable to find package Rebel.NET.Sdk\", your "
"NuGet configuration may be incorrect and need to be fixed."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_basics.rst:164
msgid ""
"A simple way to fix the NuGet configuration file is to regenerate it. In a "
"file explorer window, go to ``%AppData%\\NuGet``. Rename or delete the "
"``NuGet.Config`` file. When you build your Rebel project again, the file "
"will be automatically created with default values."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_basics.rst:170
msgid "Creating a C# script"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_basics.rst:172
msgid ""
"After you successfully set up C# for Rebel Editor, you should see the "
"following option when selecting **Attach Script** in the context menu of a "
"node in your scene:"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_basics.rst:177
msgid ""
"Note that while some specifics change, most concepts work the same when "
"using C# for scripting. If you're new to Rebel, you may want to follow the "
"tutorials on :doc:`/getting_started/step_by_step/scripting_languages` at "
"this point. While some places in the documentation still lack C# examples, "
"most concepts can be transferred easily from GDScript."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_basics.rst:184
msgid "Project setup and workflow"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_basics.rst:186
msgid ""
"When you create the first C# script, Rebel Editor initializes the C# project "
"files for your Rebel project. This includes generating a C# solution (``."
"sln``) and a project file (``.csproj``), as well as some utility files and "
"folders (``.mono`` and ``Properties/AssemblyInfo.cs``). All of these but ``."
"mono`` are important and should be committed to your version control system. "
"``.mono`` can be safely added to the ignore list of your VCS. When "
"troubleshooting, it can sometimes help to delete the ``.mono`` folder and "
"let it regenerate."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_basics.rst:198
msgid ""
"Here's a blank C# script with some comments to demonstrate how it works."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_basics.rst:225
msgid ""
"As you can see, functions normally in global scope in GDScript like Rebel "
"Engine's ``print`` function are available in the ``GD`` class which is part "
"of the ``Rebel`` namespace. For a list of methods in the ``GD`` class, see "
"the API documentation pages for :ref:`@GDScript <class_@gdscript>` and :ref:"
"`@GlobalScope <class_@globalscope>`."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_basics.rst:232
msgid ""
"Keep in mind that the class you wish to attach to your node should have the "
"same name as the ``.cs`` file. Otherwise, you will get the following error "
"and won't be able to run the scene: *\"Cannot find class XXX for script "
"res://XXX.cs\"*"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_basics.rst:238
msgid "General differences between C# and GDScript"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_basics.rst:240
msgid ""
"The C# API uses ``PascalCase`` instead of ``snake_case`` in GDScript/C++. "
"Where possible, fields and getters/setters have been converted to "
"properties. In general, the C# Rebel Engine API strives to be as idiomatic "
"as is reasonably possible."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_basics.rst:244
msgid "For more information, see the :doc:`c_sharp_differences` page."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_basics.rst:248
msgid ""
"You need to (re)build the project assemblies whenever you want to see new "
"exported variables or signals in the editor. This build can be manually "
"triggered by clicking the word **Build** in the top right corner of the "
"editor. You can also click **Mono** at the bottom of the editor window to "
"reveal the Mono panel, then click the **Build Project** button."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_basics.rst:254
msgid ""
"You will also need to rebuild the project assemblies to apply changes in "
"\"tool\" scripts."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_basics.rst:258
msgid "Current gotchas and known issues"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_basics.rst:260
msgid ""
"As C# support is quite new in Rebel Engine, there are some growing pains and "
"things that need to be ironed out. Below is a list of the most important "
"issues you should be aware of when diving into C# in Rebel Engine:"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_basics.rst:264
msgid ""
"Writing editor plugins is possible, but it is currently quite convoluted."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_basics.rst:265
msgid ""
"State is currently not saved and restored when hot-reloading, with the "
"exception of exported variables."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_basics.rst:267
msgid ""
"Attached C# scripts should refer to a class that has a class name that "
"matches the file name."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_basics.rst:269
msgid ""
"There are some methods such as ``Get()``/``Set()``, ``Call()``/"
"``CallDeferred()`` and signal connection method ``Connect()`` that rely on "
"Rebel Engine's ``snake_case`` API naming conventions. So when using e.g. "
"``CallDeferred(\"AddChild\")``, ``AddChild`` will not work because the API "
"is expecting the original ``snake_case`` version ``add_child``. However, you "
"can use any custom properties or methods without this limitation."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_basics.rst:277
msgid ""
"Exporting Mono projects is supported for desktop platforms (Linux, Windows "
"and macOS), Android, HTML5, and iOS. The only platform not supported yet is "
"UWP."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_basics.rst:281
msgid "Performance of C# in Rebel Engine"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_basics.rst:283
msgid ""
"According to some preliminary `benchmarks <https://github.com/cart/godot3-"
"bunnymark>`__, the performance of C# in Rebel Engine — while generally in "
"the same order of magnitude — is roughly **~4×** that of GDScript in some "
"naive cases. C++ is still a little faster; the specifics are going to vary "
"according to your use case. GDScript is likely fast enough for most general "
"scripting workloads. C# is faster, but requires some expensive marshalling "
"when talking to Rebel Engine."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_basics.rst:291
msgid "Using NuGet packages in Rebel Engine"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_basics.rst:293
msgid ""
"`NuGet <https://www.nuget.org/>`__ packages can be installed and used with "
"Rebel Engine, as with any C# project. Many IDEs are able to add packages "
"directly. They can also be added manually by adding the package reference in "
"the ``.csproj`` file located in the project root:"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_basics.rst:307
msgid ""
"Rebel Editor automatically downloads and sets up newly added NuGet packages "
"the next time it builds the project."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_basics.rst:311
msgid "Profiling your C# code"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_basics.rst:313
msgid ""
"`Mono log profiler <https://www.mono-project.com/docs/debug+profile/profile/"
"profiler/>`__ is available for Linux and macOS. Due to a Mono change, it "
"does not work on Windows currently."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_basics.rst:314
msgid ""
"External Mono profiler like `JetBrains dotTrace <https://www.jetbrains.com/"
"profiler/>`__ can be used as described `here <https://github.com/godotengine/"
"godot/pull/34382>`__."
msgstr ""

