"As explained in the :doc:`/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_basics`, C# "
"generally uses ``PascalCase`` instead of the ``snake_case`` used in GDScript "
"and C++."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_differences.rst:15
msgid ""
"Global functions and some constants had to be moved to classes, since C# "
"does not allow declaring them in namespaces. Most global constants were "
"moved to their own enums."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_differences.rst:22
msgid ""
"Global constants were moved to their own enums. For example, ``ERR_*`` "
"constants were moved to the ``Error`` enum."
