msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/gdscript/gdscript_styleguide.rst:571
msgid ""
"Prepend a single underscore (\\_) to virtual methods functions the user must "
"override, private functions, and private variables:"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/gdscript/gdscript_styleguide.rst:582
msgid "Use the past tense to name signals:"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/gdscript/gdscript_styleguide.rst:590
msgid "Constants and enums"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/gdscript/gdscript_styleguide.rst:592
#: tutorials/shaders/shaders_style_guide.rst:307
msgid ""
"Write constants with CONSTANT\\_CASE, that is to say in all caps with an "
"underscore (\\_) to separate words:"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/gdscript/gdscript_styleguide.rst:599
msgid ""
"Use PascalCase for enum *names* and CONSTANT\\_CASE for their members, as "
"they are constants:"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/gdscript/gdscript_styleguide.rst:613
#: tutorials/shaders/shaders_style_guide.rst:315
msgid "Code order"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/gdscript/gdscript_styleguide.rst:615
msgid ""
"This first section focuses on code order. For formatting, see :ref:"
"`formatting`. For naming conventions, see :ref:`naming_conventions`."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/gdscript/gdscript_styleguide.rst:618
msgid "We suggest to organize GDScript code this way:"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/gdscript/gdscript_styleguide.rst:641
#: tutorials/shaders/shaders_style_guide.rst:334
msgid ""
"We optimized the order to make it easy to read the code from top to bottom, "
"to help developers reading the code for the first time understand how it "
"works, and to avoid errors linked to the order of variable declarations."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/gdscript/gdscript_styleguide.rst:645
msgid "This code order follows four rules of thumb:"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/gdscript/gdscript_styleguide.rst:647
msgid "Properties and signals come first, followed by methods."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/gdscript/gdscript_styleguide.rst:648
msgid "Public comes before private."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/gdscript/gdscript_styleguide.rst:649
msgid "Virtual callbacks come before the class's interface."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/gdscript/gdscript_styleguide.rst:650
msgid ""
"The object's construction and initialization functions, ``_init`` and "
"``_ready``, come before functions that modify the object at runtime."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/gdscript/gdscript_styleguide.rst:655
msgid "Class declaration"
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/gdscript/gdscript_styleguide.rst:657
msgid ""
"If the code is meant to run in the editor, place the ``tool`` keyword on the "
"first line of the script."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/gdscript/gdscript_styleguide.rst:660
msgid ""
"Follow with the `class_name` if necessary. You can turn a GDScript file into "
"a global type in your project using this feature. For more information, see :"
"doc:`/tutorials/scripting/gdscript/gdscript_basics`."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/gdscript/gdscript_styleguide.rst:664
msgid "Then, add the `extends` keyword if the class extends a built-in type."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/gdscript/gdscript_styleguide.rst:666
msgid ""
"Following that, you should have the class's optional docstring as comments. "
"You can use that to explain the role of your class to your teammates, how it "
"works, and how other developers should use it, for example."
msgstr ""

#: tutorials/scripting/gdscript/gdscript_styleguide.rst:678
msgid "Signals and properties"
msgstr ""

